{
  "FormatVersion": 3,
  "Id": "d4d3c22e-754e-41f3-9eaf-c90c94309cc8",
  "Description": "A [RigidJoint] of type Weld turns two bodies into one rigid assembly: the pairs here tumble and land as single dumbbells instead of separating.\n\nOnly the welded pairs keep their distance under impact; Local Offset B is the offset of the second body's origin in the first one's frame, which is what makes the two act as one piece.\n\nAKA: weld, rigid joint, constraint, compound body\n\nTips\n- Use a Weld joint to fake compound colliders out of simple shapes.\n- Change Joint Type on a [RigidJoint] to Hinge for a door, or Distance Servo to keep a gap.\n- Set Reset on [PhysicsWorld] to drop the assembly again.",
